hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19196","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution sniff water, and when you clean with stones use odd."
"19197","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution sniff water, and when you clean with stones use odd."
"19198","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at the Farewell Hajj: They are only four: Associate nothing with Allah, kill not the soul Allah forbade except by right, steal not, and fornicate not."
"19199","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays al-Ashjai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at the Farewell Hajj: Lo, they are only four: That you associate nothing with Allah, kill not the soul Allah forbade except by right, fornicate not, and steal not. He said: I am not more careful of them than I since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19200","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar and al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you perform ablution sniff water, and when you clean with stones use odd."
